blies/*.dll|*.blob, libmonodroid.so   Xamarin: XALZ = lz4 per-dll; then ilspycmd f.dll\n   libil2cpp.so + global-metadata.dat         Unity IL2CPP: strings global-metadata.dat | grep ANS- ; Managed/*.dll -> ilspycmd\n   assets/www/, cordova.js, capacitor.config  hybrid JS: grep -r in assets/www\n   assets/*.dex|*.jar|*.apk|*.zip|*.bin       dynamic code loading: unzip it, jadx it, re-run extract_answer on it\n   libjiagu/libsecexe/libDexHelper.so          packer: payload is the encrypted asset; static decrypt or give up early\n   res/xml/network_security_config.xml        NSC: aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/network_security_config.xml\n   resources.arsc                   aapt dump --values resources x.apk | grep -iE 'ans-|secret|key|flag|token'\n   *.db / shared_prefs/*.xml / *.ab sqlite3 f.db .dump ; .ab: dd bs=24 skip=1 | zlib-flate -uncompress | tar x\n   res/raw/*.bks|*.p12|*.pem        keystore: password is a dex string; keytool -list -v -storepass PW\n   google-services.json / firebase  key/URL itself may be the answer\n   base.apk + split_config.*.apk / manifest.json / toc.pb / BundleConfig.pb   split/XAPK/APKS/AAB: unzip inner, recurse\n   Payload/*.app/                   iOS: plistlib Info.plist; rz-bin -zz the Mach-O\n2. Plain-anywhere scan (incl. UTF-16 the zip scan misses):\n   for f in $(unzip -Z1 x.apk); do unzip -p x.apk \"$f\" | strings -a -el | grep -H --label=\"$f\" ANS-; done\n   7z l x.apk vs unzip -l x.apk differ -> zip tricks (dup entry / trailing data): binwalk x.apk\n3. Manifest (fast): aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml | grep -E \\\n   'exported|scheme|host|autoVerify|permission|debuggable|allowBackup|usesCleartext|networkSecurity|taskAffinity|launchMode|meta-data'\n   meta-data value= is a hiding spot (huntress.mechanic lives there). droidasc getmanifest x.apk prints the XML.\n4. Dex triage: strings -a classes*.dex | grep -E 'DAY-|CODEC|ANS-|^[0-9A-F]{8,16}$' then map API hits to themes:\n   DexClassLoader/InMemoryDexClassLoader -> asset dex     SecretKeySpec/AES/Cipher/IvParameterSpec -> static key decrypt\n   loadLibrary/RegisterNatives -> .so                     java/util/Random/setSeed/currentTimeMillis -> regenerate RNG\n   MessageDigest/PBKDF2 -> hash brute                     addJavascriptInterface/loadUrl/file:///android_asset -> assets html/js\n   Binder/$Stub/Messenger/onReceive -> IPC handler        CertificatePinner/sha256/ -> pins in code or NSC\n   su/magisk/RootBeer/goldfish/frida/TracerPid -> flag sits in the gated branch: read it, never run it\n   Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod -> decode names        BuildConfig / R$string -> arsc / BuildConfig.java\n   KeyStore.getInstance(\"BKS\"|\"PKCS12\") -> res/raw keystore + password string\n5. Read code only after 1-4: droidasc findrefs x.apk string <hit>; droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>; jadx -d w/jadx x.apk\n   (add --deobf for 1-2 letter class names). Strings split across constants: rebuild order from the method body.\n   R8/decoys (D17): hint strings like \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\" name the chain; >1 ANS- candidate -> keep\n   the one appended before `proof=` in ChallengeActivity, never the first regex hit.\n6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n7. Validate: candidate must fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). Two sources (asset + .so) agreeing = submit.\n8. Mastery: each set can be a different day's fixture; decode every APK on its own; loop over all answer_ids (3 or 5).\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\nutf16-string-pool-scan, nested-container-recurse, dex-native-split-assembly, static-key-cipher-decode, decode-any-\nchain-peel, native-so-emulate-export, dex-string-decrypt-arrays, asset-db-prefs-backup, identity-derived-key, hermes-\nhbc-string-table, cert-and-signing-facts, il2cpp-metadata-literals, jni-export-return-trace, jni-gate-bypass-input,\nregisternatives-table, native-stack-string, multi-abi-arm-native, dex-native-call-args, native-gated-branch-read, dex-\ngated-branch-consts, webview-asset-js-scan, cert-pin-and-nsc-facts.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields\", \"concept\": \"permutation codecs keyed by an int list (rows 36; D17 `indexed`, D5/D10 `split`)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17's race probe failed because lib.android.puzzle_candidates has no `indexed`. Add to decode_payload/puzzle_candidates: for ANY puzzle JSON whose codec is unknown or `indexed`/`perm*`/`shuffle*`, take every int-list field (order/perm/index/positions/map/slots) of len(data) or len(parts) and try scatter (r[o[i]]=d[i]) and gather (d[o[i]]), also 1-based and inverse; keep the ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ match. Regression: the three d17 APKs (single, TT, Mastery set 5).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"proof-flow-candidate-ranking\", \"concept\": \"decoy insertion: several ANS- candidates, code picks one (row 67)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"androguard, pure python: in ChallengeActivity (or whichever method const-strings `proof=`/`evidence?`), walk the StringBuilder.append chain and resolve the register appended after `proof=` back to its source (const-string, sget of a static field -> its <clinit> sput value, invoke of a renamed getter returning a const or a field). Return that value, plus the full candidate list with a `reached_by_proof` flag so solve.py prefers it over the first regex hit when the asset/dex/.so offer more than one ANS- value.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"r8-renamed-chain-follow\", \"concept\": \"R8-renamed class chain (row 45; D17 TT hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c`)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"androguard: index every 1-2 letter class in the app package; build field->value (static initialisers, constructor iput of consts) and method->return-const maps; follow invoke/sget chains from ChallengeActivity.onCreate through renamed classes (depth <= 6). Parse dex hint strings of the form `follow X -> Y`, `ignore field Z` and apply them (skip Z, prefer Y's value). Feeds decode_any for each reached value. Covers the day the answer moves from the asset into a renamed class.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dalvik-mini-interpreter\", \"concept\": \"answer computed by simple dex bytecode (char arrays, xor/add loops, StringBuilder, switch-flattened control flow) (rows 35, 43, 45)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Tiny pure-python Dalvik evaluator over androguard instructions for ONE method: const*/move*/aget/aput/fill-array-data/new-array/arith-int(lit)/if-*/goto/packed-switch + intrinsics String.<init>([C), StringBuilder.append/toString, String.charAt/length/getBytes, Integer.parseInt, Base64.decode. Step budget 50k, unknown invokes -> abort. Run it on static String-returning methods and on the proof= builder; regex the results. Handles string-encryption helpers and control-flow flattening without a device.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"permutation-transposition-family\", \"concept\": \"keyless/known-plaintext transposition codecs (row 36)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"When a puzzle `data` is 20 chars containing exactly one each of A,N,S,- but no index list: derive the permutation from the known prefix and the public shape -- stride/affine slot map (i*k+o mod n, D17's order was (3+7i) mod 20), rail-fence (2-5 rails), columnar with width 2-10, even/odd interleave, chunk-reverse. Each family has <= ~200 parameter choices fixed by where A,N,S,- sit; keep only outputs matching ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ and require a unique match (a decode, never a submit loop).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"reflection-name-resolve\", \"concept\": \"Class.forName / getDeclaredField / getDeclaredMethod with encoded names (row 43)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"androguard: find invokes of Class.forName, getDeclaredField/Method, Field.get, Method.invoke; resolve their String args (const-string, or via dalvik-mini-interpreter for decoded names), map to the real class/field in the dex and return that field's static value. Natural next step after R8 renaming in a resilience arc.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"proguard-mapping-restore\", \"concept\": \"restore original names: mapping.txt / kotlin Metadata / SourceFile (row 45)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If a question asks 'what was class a / method b originally' or the APK ships assets/mapping.txt|*.map|seeds.txt: parse the ProGuard mapping format (`orig.Class -> a:` + indented `type orig -> b` members) and kotlin.Metadata d2 string arrays + dex SourceFile/debug_info names; expose renamed->original facts and look up hint strings (`follow b -> a`) by original name.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"apk-signing-block-payload\", \"concept\": \"hidden data in the APK Signing Block id-value pairs (rows 59, 62)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every fixture has an APK Signing Block. Pure python: locate EOCD -> central dir offset -> `APK Sig Block 42` magic, walk the uint64-length id-value pairs, skip 0x7109871a (v2), 0xf05368c0 (v3), 0x1b93ad61 (v3.1), 0x42726577 (padding), 0x6dff800d (source stamp); return the other values (channel ids like Walle 0x71777777) and regex/decode_any them. Cheap hiding spot no extractor reads yet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"zip-structure-anomaly-scan\", \"concept\": \"ZIP-level tricks: duplicate names, local vs central mismatch, data after EOCD, archive comment, extra fields (row 62)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Pure python walk of local file headers independently of the central directory: report entries present only locally, duplicate names (Android takes the first; zipfile the last), differing sizes/names between local and central records, bytes between entries or after EOCD, the archive comment and non-standard extra fields; feed each blob to raw_entry_scan/decode_any. Catches a decoy entry shadowing the real puzzle JSON.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/37830cfa-6824-4c93-b6b0-10dc17668190/tool-results/b1nmzyfga.txt","persistedOutputSize":33029},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013dbYda5rUue61m8aZaNGkN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
